        "id": "intro-comment",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Gate Out the Room Noise\n\nSilences audio that falls below a threshold, so the hiss between phrases disappears and the phrases themselves stay untouched.\n\n**How it works:** \"Audio\" passes the recording to \"Gate\". Anything quieter than -45 dB is muted. A 1 ms attack opens the gate quickly when speech starts, and a 120 ms release closes it smoothly afterward. \"Result\" shows the gated audio. It is local audio processing with no model.\n\n**Try this:** If quiet word endings get clipped, lower the threshold on \"Gate\" to -55 dB or raise the release to 250 ms."
        },
